WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.154 --> 00:00:03.528
(slow upbeat hip-hop music)

00:00:03.528 --> 00:00:08.010
- [Swerte] Hip-hop is the
fastest growing culture, period.

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:10.254
People who don't believe that
there's hip-hop in Dubai,

00:00:10.254 --> 00:00:14.156
or anywhere else in the world,
have been hiding in a cave.

00:00:14.156 --> 00:00:16.239
(laughs)

00:00:21.853 --> 00:00:24.123
- My name is P. Storm,
I'm English and Chinese.

00:00:24.123 --> 00:00:26.467
- I'm Swerte, I'm Indonesian/Swiss.

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:27.815
- My name's Kaz Money,

00:00:27.815 --> 00:00:31.099
I'm Armenian/Syrian, Italian/Eritrean.

00:00:31.099 --> 00:00:33.260
We are The Recipe.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.018
(intense rapping)

00:00:36.018 --> 00:00:37.778
- [Female Narrator] In
2008, The Recipe began

00:00:37.778 --> 00:00:39.361
as a compilation project

00:00:39.361 --> 00:00:42.878
featuring 14 different artists
and producers in the UAE.

00:00:42.878 --> 00:00:44.853
Today, the remaining
three members are building

00:00:44.853 --> 00:00:47.600
a true hip-hop movement
in the Middle East.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:49.867
- The hip-hop scene's
really young in Dubai,

00:00:49.867 --> 00:00:52.395
it is very unlike any
other scene in the world

00:00:52.395 --> 00:00:56.125
because a majority of the
population are ex-pats,

00:00:56.125 --> 00:00:57.667
and this is a transient city,

00:00:57.667 --> 00:01:01.300
so it is a very fast-paced culture.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:03.884
It's probably the first place
where I really feel home.

00:01:03.884 --> 00:01:07.191
Some place where I really feel accepted.

00:01:07.191 --> 00:01:09.658
- I think what makes The
Recipe unique is we all

00:01:09.658 --> 00:01:11.774
live in a country that
we're not really from,

00:01:11.774 --> 00:01:14.114
so we bring different
perspectives, and it really does

00:01:14.114 --> 00:01:16.771
play a big role in the
music that we do create.

00:01:16.771 --> 00:01:17.832
- (rapping) ♫ I leave you
looney with these tunes,

00:01:17.832 --> 00:01:20.116
♫ That's all folks

00:01:20.116 --> 00:01:21.848
(spoken) Done!

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:23.564
- [Female Narrator] The
Recipe is breaking stereotypes

00:01:23.564 --> 00:01:24.926
about the Middle East by showing the world

00:01:24.926 --> 00:01:27.510
through their music that
hip-hop is truly global.

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:30.206
- Hey yo, it's Talib Kweli,
we with The Recipe right now,

00:01:30.206 --> 00:01:31.039
- Yeah boy!

00:01:31.039 --> 00:01:32.747
- Karama, you know what I'm saying?

00:01:32.747 --> 00:01:33.755
Dubai, you know what I'm saying?

00:01:33.755 --> 00:01:35.705
- [Female Narrator] Even
rap legends like Talib Kweli

00:01:35.705 --> 00:01:37.549
and Mobb Deep are taking notice.

00:01:37.549 --> 00:01:40.707
(fast rapping)

00:01:40.707 --> 00:01:42.336
- ♫ And we breakin through,
gonna make it through

00:01:42.336 --> 00:01:44.777
- [P. Storm] Hip-Hop is
really storytelling.

00:01:44.777 --> 00:01:46.018
- ♫ But this is like, stuck in a place

00:01:46.018 --> 00:01:47.576
♫ That I call my home,
but it don't play me,

00:01:47.576 --> 00:01:48.937
♫ Cuz I can't move, right

00:01:48.937 --> 00:01:52.134
- We really respect the craft,
so we're always inspired

00:01:52.134 --> 00:01:55.643
to be better writers,
to be better lyricists.

00:01:55.643 --> 00:01:57.421
♫ I'm living this life, playing this part

00:01:57.421 --> 00:01:58.696
♫ That you really want, right?

00:01:58.696 --> 00:02:00.404
♫ Acting this way that
you really gonna like,

00:02:00.404 --> 00:02:02.382
♫ Got a contract, sign
for this ignorant type

00:02:02.382 --> 00:02:06.580
- The goal was always
just to do what we love,

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:09.407
and thankfully by doing
that, we've been able to

00:02:09.407 --> 00:02:12.639
achieve and experience what we've done.

00:02:12.639 --> 00:02:15.316
- Up to this point, we've
imported everything.

00:02:15.316 --> 00:02:18.253
Hopefully the world starts to
recognize and look at Dubai

00:02:18.253 --> 00:02:20.292
as a viable source of music.

00:02:20.292 --> 00:02:22.784
Somewhere that you can
look to to get music

00:02:22.784 --> 00:02:25.617
that you actually would listen to.

